00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:02.400
platforms like Questrade using the 5-10-year treasury segment and rebalance quarterly against

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:10.620
your RRSP target. The approach worked best in 2022-2023 when duration driven volatility rewarded

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:17.060
those who shortened exposure ahead of policy shifts. Risk lies in misjudging inflation persistence

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:23.620
which could extend to draw downs. Duration management is one piece of a broader allocation approach

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:30.440
will unpack next. Imagine you bought XEQT last month, expecting broad equity exposure,

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:37.540
only to watch a single sector rotation cut your monthly return by 1.8% while bonds held steady.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:44.500
The mechanism at work is modern portfolio theory's core math. Combining assets with low correlation

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:51.060
reduces portfolio standard deviation without lowering expected return, moving you closer to the

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:57.760
efficient frontier where risk adjusted returns peak. Professionals always check the 36-month rolling

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:03.540
correlation matrix between equities, bonds, and alternatives before adding a new ETF,

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:11.640
something retail investors skip when chasing recent winners. Canadian examples show VGRO delivering

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:18.680
smoother draw downs than pure equity during the 2022 rate hike cycle because it's 20% fixed income

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:25.540
sleeve offset equity losses. The biggest mistake with asset allocation is treating age-based rules

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:32.540
like 100-year-age in stocks as fixed rather than starting points. Instead, always run a quick

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:38.800
risk tolerance questionnaire on your brokerage site and set rebalancing bands at 5% drift from

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:44.700
targets using calendar or threshold methods while tracking probabilities, three quick developments

